@startuml act_low_beam
title Activity - Activate low beam including the fault case (SYS-REQ-001, FSR-001)

start
:Receive LightRequest = low\nfrom Vehicle_Gateway;
if (Request valid and not timed out?) then (yes)
  :SWC_LightManager commands\nPWM and enable to LED_Driver_Stage_1;
  :LED driver regulates channel\nto the commanded set point;
  repeat
    :Current_Sense_Chain samples\nI_load in the PWM on-phase;
    note right
      Source of the decision criteria below
      (all values are plausible examples):
      * 150 mA / 50 ms threshold: SYS-REQ-014,
        realised by SM-01 in Current_Sense_Chain
        (HW-REQ-002, debounce HW-REQ-009)
      * 150 us minimum on-time: blanking and
        conversion budget, HW-REQ-003. Below it the
        diagnosis is reported "not available"
        (SYS-REQ-017, decision OP-17); HW-REQ-004 is
        not implemented in the base variant
      * measurement uncertainty +/-20 mA at the
        threshold: SYS-REQ-016 / HW-REQ-001
      Tolerance chain and timing budget:
      05_hardware/analysis_current_sensing.md
      Sampling raster assumes A-08 (1.20 A nominal)
      and A-09 (400 Hz PWM, duty >= 20 %).
    end note
    if (PWM on-time >= 150 us?) then (yes)
      if (I_load < 150 mA for > 50 ms?) then (yes)
        :Debounce 20 ms;
        :Discriminate cause\n(SYS-REQ-019);
        if (Cause = open load?) then (yes)
          :Classify channel as "open load"\n(SYS-REQ-014); <<#FFDDDD>>
          :Enter safe state: operate remaining\nchannel, set DTC (TSR-004); <<#FFDDDD>>
          :Request driver warning\nwithin 2 s (FSR-004); <<#FFDDDD>>
          stop
        else (no)
          :Handle as short-to-battery\nor commanded reduction;
        endif
      else (no)
        :Channel healthy;
      endif
    else (no)
      :Report diagnosis\n"not available" (SYS-REQ-017);
    endif
  repeat while (Low beam still requested?) is (yes)
  ->no;
  :De-energise channel;
else (no)
  :Keep previous state,\nset communication DTC;
endif
stop
@enduml
